<Page title="Cookie Policy — Nairon" description="How Nairon uses cookies on our website: essential and functional cookies, Google Analytics 4 for traffic measurement, and how to opt out." eyebrow="Legal" heading="Cookie Policy" intro="This policy explains what cookies are, which cookies our website uses, and how you can control them." updated="July 25, 2026">
  <div class="page-body">
    <div class="page-prose">
      <h2>What cookies are</h2>
      <p>Cookies are small text files that a website stores on your device when you visit. They let the site remember basic information about your visit, such as your preferences or how you arrived on a page. Some cookies are set by us. Others are set by third-party services we use, such as our analytics provider.</p>
      <p>Cookies can last for a single session or for a set period. Session cookies are removed when you close your browser. Persistent cookies stay on your device until they expire or you delete them.</p>

      <h2>The cookies we use</h2>
      <p>Our website uses a small number of cookies. We group them into the categories below.</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Essential</strong> &mdash; Required for the website to load and function. These support core delivery and security. The site does not work correctly without them, so they cannot be turned off through a consent choice.</li>
        <li><strong>Functional</strong> &mdash; Remember basic preferences so the site behaves consistently across pages during your visit.</li>
        <li><strong>Analytics</strong> &mdash; Help us understand how visitors use the site, so we can measure traffic and improve pages. See the section below for detail.</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Analytics: Google Analytics 4</h3>
      <p>We use Google Analytics 4 to measure website traffic and understand which pages people visit. This helps us see how the site is performing and where to improve it. Google Analytics sets the following cookies on your device:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>_ga</strong> &mdash; Distinguishes one visitor from another so that visits can be counted.</li>
        <li><strong>_ga_*</strong> &mdash; A per-property cookie (the name ends with your Google Analytics property identifier) used to keep session state.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>These cookies collect aggregate usage data such as page views and general session information. We use this data to measure traffic, not to identify you personally.</p>

      <h2>We do not use advertising cookies</h2>
      <p>We do not use advertising or marketing cookies. We do not use cookies to build advertising profiles, retarget you across other websites, or sell your data to advertisers. Our cookie use is limited to running the site and measuring traffic.</p>

      <h2>Managing and opting out of cookies</h2>
      <p>You can control cookies in two ways:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Browser settings</strong> &mdash; Every major browser lets you view, block, and delete cookies. Check your browser&rsquo;s help pages for instructions. Blocking essential cookies may stop parts of the site from working.</li>
        <li><strong>Google Analytics opt-out</strong> &mdash; To opt out of Google Analytics across all websites, install the Google Analytics Opt-out Browser Add-on: <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout">https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout</a>.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>We may update this Cookie Policy from time to time, for example if we change the services we use or add new cookies. When we do, we will revise the date shown at the top of this page. We encourage you to review this page periodically.</p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>If you have questions about this Cookie Policy or how we use cookies, contact us at <a href="mailto:hello@naironai.com">hello@naironai.com</a> or write to Nairon, 2125 Biscayne Blvd, Miami, FL 33137.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Page>
